  "functions": [
    "FUNC.ISREF"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "ISREF inspects reference identity without reading cell values (returning TRUE on error cells), and returns FALSE for #REF! and arrays",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, ISREF(value) tests whether value is a reference without dereferencing or reading cells—returning TRUE for single cells, multi-cell ranges, area unions such as (A1,B2), cells holding an error (=ISREF(B7) -> TRUE), and reference-preserving IF calls (=ISREF(IF(TRUE,Data!A1:A3,0)) -> TRUE), and returning FALSE for numbers, text such as \"A1\", literal #REF!, and arrays such as {1}. Matches 1,227/1,227 full-bank and 120/120 pinned rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20527.20196 (dc_nzpw rows 91-98), Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (fn2_questions fn2_q023, fn2_q024, fn2_q030; jnt_parse_bind rows 15-17), and 1,227/1,227 full-bank and 120/120 pinned rows (ISREF.json).",
